silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_08_cross_paper_bridges_sections_02_bridge_to_19_mereology_yoneda_hom_leg silm:hasExample "In 'BridgeTo19MereologyYonedaHomLeg', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, paper 19's typed mereological leg. the transport functor F preserves this typed leg in the Mittens vet-clinic migration; the household-side arrow is named and the clinic-side image is named, with arrow direction and typing kept intact.; also, the clinic-side image of the cocone leg. the transport functor F preserves this typed leg in the Mittens vet-clinic migration; the household-side arrow is named and the clinic-side image is named, with arrow direction and typing kept intact." .
